      "side_effects": [
        "Attempt journal, one protocol report and, from 1.6.0, bounded research requests to Control Center (inside its daily caps; it may file a commenter as a cold, engaged contact); a public read of krishraja.com's own repository for the track record a pitch quotes; never a message, post, spend, Gmail draft or Advisory batch (from 1.9.0 Control Center drafts the pitches into Jonny's Gmail itself)"
      ],
      "retry": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "total_attempt_cap": 1,
        "checkpoint": "Control Center report journal keyed by the stable run_id; read back before any repeat, a 409 is read back and never resent",
        "recovery_entrypoint": "dispatch-recovery"
      },
      "completion": {
        "source": "destination_readback",
        "evidence": "tests/dispatch.test.mjs verifies the started and terminal attempts, the report digest readback, replay, conflict and decisions against a local stand-in; tests/rows.test.mjs verifies the five rows, the live canon read, the signal pipeline and that only counts are printed; tests/pitches.test.mjs verifies the 1.9.0 podcast and speaking pitches and the guest invites onto his shows for Jonny's Gmail; tests/network.test.mjs verifies that no one inside his network, or whom Control Center cannot place, is given a Jonny action, and that the same invite or pitch goes on his own row instead; the invites' weekly shares, their shared budget, the live track record read and that they are written only where Control Center serves 1.9.0; tests/forms.test.mjs verifies the stage forms for his Submit: each field answered by its own label, the holds that leave a form unwritten and fall to the pitch, a try that sent nothing routed again, and that every action parses as Control Center reads it; tests/spec.test.mjs verifies the week spec: the default spec reproduces today's caps, a signed spec (his Clear or his digest-verified version) compiles inside config/policy.json's bounds and reaches the stages, the spec_too_long, spec_amended_invalid and spec_unsigned holds, the fallback chain, Jonny's ten drafts a day across wakes, and that no spec can loosen a bound or add spend; tests/golden/ holds every earlier fixture's report digest, checked byte for byte; tests/crew.test.mjs verifies each specialist's lint and measured check, card grammar over every live failure shape and its generated variants, and that the crew in shadow changes no proposal; tests/library.test.mjs verifies the Growth library taxonomy and check; tests/guests.test.mjs, tests/visibility.test.mjs and tests/rooms.test.mjs verify the guest standard, the shows' split and queue, the visibility standard and room scoring ported from Control Center (plan section 12, M3 to M5), each against Control Center's own cases, and that their shadow functions read the context, change nothing and report counts only; tests/pilots.test.mjs, tests/briefs.test.mjs and tests/ingest-gate.test.mjs verify the pilot machine, the People briefs and the legacy ingest gate ported from Control Center (plan section 12, M6, M9 and M12) against Control Center's own answers and the canon read live; tests/plays.test.mjs, tests/suppression.test.mjs and tests/places.test.mjs verify the focus playbooks, the taxonomy and the suppression of his Nos, and the places and questions ported from Control Center (plan section 12, M7, M10 and M13) against Control Center's own rules, the suppression in a 500-case sweep and every difference by code; tests/section12.test.mjs verifies on the stand-in that each of the nine section 12 lines is reported once, in counts only, holding nothing, with the switch's line still after them, and that a fault in one never fails the run; tests/regression/ holds the regression tests for F08, F10, F15, F18, F21 and F48 and the N02, N06 and N09 findings; tests/switch.test.mjs verifies the Phase 5 switch: one readiness line every run, the crew enforcing only from this week's signed spec with enabled, five proof runs, the shadow lines and the number measured, never from an unsigned spec or the fallback, and the old route kept 30 days after the switch tests/credits.test.mjs verifies that credits are read only where served, that a spend past the share is refused before it runs and that a report carrying credits_spent is 1.16.0 and passes the stand-in."
      }
    }
